{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And your enemies shall be appalled at it.</b> It shall be a desolation to your enemies — they shall find no gratification in it. And this is good tidings for Israel, and so the Rabbis, blessed be their memory, expounded in Torat Kohanim: 'This is a good measure for Israel, lest Israel say: since we have been exiled from our land, now the enemies come and find gratification in it — as it is said, ״ושממו עליה אויביכם היושבים בה״ — even the enemies who come after you shall find no gratification in it,' end quote. From this he said that even those who dwell in it shall deal desolately with it — they shall not build upon it a wall and a tower, and all the nations shall strive to build it but have no power. And in this there is a great sign for Israel: from the day it was destroyed it has received no nation and tongue, nor shall it receive any until its children return to its midst."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:51.653467171Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}